WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Welcome to this course focused on getting started with Model Contacts Protocol.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.000
My name is Stephen Greider and I'll be guiding you through everything you need to know around MCP.

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Let's first begin by understanding exactly what we'll cover in the coming videos.

4
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:18.000
We'll first get an overview on MCP and understand what problems it is intended to solve.

5
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:25.000
We'll then start to look at the basics of MCP architecture by covering the responsibilities of MCP clients and servers.

6
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Then it is on to the three basic components of an MCP server.

7
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:33.000
First, we'll look at tools, which are intended to be consumed by language models.

8
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:38.000
After that, we'll study resources, which allow a server to share data with clients.

9
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:43.000
And finally, prompts, which will provide tuned directions to language models.

10
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Now, there's a lot of content for us to get through, so there are a couple of requirements on your side.

11
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.000
First, you need to have some basic Python knowledge.

12
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Second, we will be writing out some code, and this will require a local Python installation.

13
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:02.000
We will be managing our project with the uv-cli, and if you don't have it installed, I recommend grabbing it now.

14
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Get a link to it on the screen.